\newlabel{fig:curvature}{{1}{6}{Exact analytic functions in the two-level example. (a) The curvatures derived from the two projectors have polar integrals $+1$ and $-1$. (b) The fixed chart coefficients have equal derivatives and differ by one at every latitude. The north coefficient has pole values 0 and 1. These are analytic illustrations, not measured data; their scalar identities are checked in Lean}{figure.1}{}}
